{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "title",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Agent Client Protocol (ACP)\n\nStandardized communication between editors and AI coding agents",
      "x": 250,
      "y": -150,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "#8b5cf6",
      "pv": {
        "name": "ACP Overview"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "editor",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Code Editor / IDE\n\n**Examples:**\n- VS Code\n- Zed\n- Your Electron App\n- JetBrains\n\n**Role:** ClientSideConnection",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 50,
      "width": 250,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "#22c55e",
      "pv": {
        "icon": "Monitor",
        "shape": "rectangle",
        "name": "Editor/Client"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "agent",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# AI Coding Agent\n\n**Examples:**\n- Claude Code\n- Gemini CLI\n- Custom agents\n\n**Role:** AgentSideConnection",
      "x": 750,
      "y": 50,
      "width": 250,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "#8b5cf6",
      "pv": {
        "nodeType": "agent-session-service",
        "icon": "Cpu",
        "shape": "rectangle",
        "name": "Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "communication",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# JSON-RPC over stdio pipes\n\n**NOT PTY** - structured messages\n**Local:** stdin/stdout pipes\n**Remote:** HTTP/WebSocket (WIP)\n\n**Patterns:**\n- Notifications (agent → editor)\n- Bidirectional requests\n- Real-time streaming",
      "x": 331,
      "y": 59,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 180,
      "color": "#06b6d4",
      "pv": {
        "icon": "Zap",
        "shape": "hexagon",
        "name": "Communication Layer"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "init",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# 1. Initialization\n\n```json\n{\n  \"method\": \"initialize\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"protocolVersion\": \"1.0\",\n    \"capabilities\": {...}\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Negotiates:** Version & capabilities",
      "x": -28,
      "y": 838,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "#eab308",
      "pv": {
        "icon": "Handshake",
        "name": "Initialization"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "session",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# 2. Session Setup\n\n**Editor spawns agent:**\n- As subprocess (local)\n- As remote connection\n\n**Multiple sessions:** Supported for parallel work",
      "x": 397,
      "y": 837,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "#eab308",
      "pv": {
        "icon": "Play",
        "name": "Session"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "prompt-turn",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# 3. Prompt Turn Cycle\n\n**Flow:**\n1. User sends `session/prompt`\n2. Agent processes with LLM\n3. Agent sends `session/update`\n4. Agent requests tool execution\n5. Repeat until completion\n\n**Can be cancelled** anytime",
      "x": 837,
      "y": 837,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "#eab308",
      "pv": {
        "icon": "Repeat",
        "name": "Prompt Turn"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "benefits",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Key Benefits\n\n✅ **Standardization:** One protocol for all\n✅ **No vendor lock-in:** Mix & match\n✅ **Ecosystem growth:** Independent innovation\n✅ **Editor control:** Maintains authorization\n✅ **Multiple sessions:** Parallel workflows",
      "x": 1287,
      "y": 814,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 180,
      "color": "#22c55e",
      "pv": {
        "icon": "CheckCircle",
        "name": "Benefits"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "problem",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Problem Solved\n\n**Before ACP:**\n❌ Each editor must integrate every agent\n❌ Each agent must support every editor\n❌ N × M integrations needed\n❌ Developer lock-in\n\n**With ACP:**\n✅ N + M integrations\n✅ Any editor works with any agent",
      "x": -436,
      "y": -45,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "#ef4444",
      "pv": {
        "icon": "AlertTriangle",
        "name": "Problem"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "typescript-sdk",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# TypeScript SDK\n\n```bash\nnpm install @agentclientprotocol/sdk\n```\n\n**Classes:**\n- `AgentSideConnection` (build agents)\n- `ClientSideConnection` (build editors)\n\n**Also available:** Python, Rust, Kotlin",
      "x": 1275,
      "y": 334,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "#06b6d4",
      "pv": {
        "icon": "Code",
        "name": "SDK"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "integration-note",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Integration with Your App\n\n**Current state:**\n- Agent management ✅\n- Sessions ✅\n- Event infrastructure ✅\n\n**To add ACP:**\n1. Install `@agentclientprotocol/sdk`\n2. Create `ACPBridge.ts`\n3. Use **stdio pipes** (not nodepty)\n4. Extend agent config handlers\n5. Bridge ACP ↔ existing sessions\n6. Handle tool requests from agents",
      "x": 1279,
      "y": 583,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "#22c55e",
      "pv": {
        "icon": "Plug",
        "name": "Your Integration"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "pty-comparison",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# PTY vs ACP Communication\n\n**PTY (nodepty) - Keep for:**\n- Terminal emulation\n- Interactive shells\n- Build commands\n- Raw terminal I/O\n\n**ACP - Use for:**\n- Agent ↔ Editor communication\n- Structured JSON-RPC messages\n- Session management\n- Type-safe protocol",
      "x": -321,
      "y": 313,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 250,
      "color": "#8b5cf6",
      "pv": {
        "icon": "GitCompare",
        "name": "PTY vs ACP"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "stdio-detail",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# stdio Pipes (Not PTY!)\n\n```typescript\nspawn(agentPath, [], {\n  stdio: ['pipe', 'pipe', 'pipe']\n  // stdin, stdout, stderr\n})\n```\n\n**Why not PTY?**\n- ACP needs structured JSON\n- No terminal emulation needed\n- Type-safe messages\n- No ANSI escape codes",
      "x": 335,
      "y": 325,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 200,
      "color": "#eab308",
      "pv": {
        "icon": "Terminal",
        "name": "stdio Implementation"
      }
    }
  ],
